  "problem": "The circles ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/62bff9ae4f0299ac4cd10261ad85c8b0d7e5e39b6ea5e779eead290e4c5bba38.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/8b994afa2154f42fc39a361c03eb163e6ae83e588ebbe949028a0bc75e10b16d.svg)  intersect at points ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/65ada9c919fe5c4bee19fb4cafff28ed46a36bf6fc90b4cecf70e0fa02386ce0.svg) as shown below. What are the polar coordinates of the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/499b8f6de313125b2cf1bbd2ab7aa4c1044f542237f5abdf31b877ce5aecdaa6.svg) \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/5d7d5084d0b13c7484acdc8796bcd8584d77351befacacf84a153430b34f6fd4.png)",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the polar coordinates of the intersection points, we will solve the following system of equations for ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/907cfc4c25fd53cc279e07e970a8e68fab64a3558b575e0b3dfe1bd9cda24ccd.svg)\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/952b380a0e3dc52afe15e5cd8799eb50cb4125b726a1d540436fca0e75894d0e.svg)\nWe begin by setting the equations equal to each other and solving for ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/b98533dee87a7bd8ed4d593a2aabd517621d6ab96e40a5b2ab4a8ac1923ddac5.svg) This gives\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/ea2a71a3cb39086a94ea65088c951dbe8c0ec542b224f3bb724d8cbf27416f06.svg)\n\nSolving this equation in the interval ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/b501be2da8128f39c033d09dc0e2fc423e4df98c845acbdee221efbaa5cc6978.svg) we obtain  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/4ffc15045d598404d6a76b86de375abc74e21c66821149760272d73eca6b3190.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/2a50ea8c8351cbd27e82b2c20da9a482d093b20e039a650930857b36700968b1.svg)\n\nAlso, notice that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/8b994afa2154f42fc39a361c03eb163e6ae83e588ebbe949028a0bc75e10b16d.svg) at both intersection points.\n\nTherefore, the polar coordinates of the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/7533ad047439b7d799dd7afee5d6a7bc9f4404fbadb8c3f27ef6d3952119ff6b.svg) are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/eece868ab8c5a66a3f640d9f98b6ce38ed8659c0eef8158a55c5ce4edc1a5157.svg)",
